e=\"color:black\">\r\n  units     </span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;px&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">,)</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n    print</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">his</span><span style=\"color:black\">())</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n    dev.off</span><span style=\"color:black\">()</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  </span><span style=\"color:black\">}</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  </span><span style=\"color:black\">)</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\"><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">Encoding()</code> to the string given to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">filename</code> gives: <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">UTF-8</code><br>I tried to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">iconv</code> the string to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:C