:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:maroon\">400</span><span style=\"color:black\">,</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  units     </span><span style=\"color:black\">=</span><span style=\"color:black\"> </span><span style=\"color:maroon\">&quot;px&quot;</span><span style=\"color:black\">,)</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n    print</span><span style=\"color:black\">(</span><span style=\"color:black\">his</span><span style=\"color:black\">())</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n    dev.off</span><span style=\"color:black\">()</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  </span><span style=\"color:black\">}</span><span style=\"color:black\">\r\n  </span><span style=\"color:black\">)</span></code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\"><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">Encoding()</code> to the string given to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">filename</code> gives: <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">UTF-8</code><br>I tried to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">iconv</code> the string to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">windows-1255</code> did nothing, tried to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">iconv</code> to <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">UTF-16</code> and got an error:<code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">Embedded nul in string</code><br>How can i make sure that windows can recognize the file name encoding?<br>my <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">sessioninfo()</code> gives:</p><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;padding:10px;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(255,235,142);quotes:none;background-color:rgb(255,248,220)\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">R version 3.1.2 (2014-10-31) Platfo